  "adaptations": [
    "Native reconstruction of the supplied reference composition. All parameter values, effect names, modulation rows and audio plots come from the real processor; current-source captures must establish visual fidelity.",
    "The observatory copies real source wavetable frames, with actual source frame count/size and current position retained by the renderer. Non-wavetable algorithms use their native waveform preview. This is a source-table view, not an output spectrum.",
    "OSC 1/2/3 tabs select the actual source displayed by the observatory and rebind its seven dynamic parameter controls. Selection changes view state without changing the sound.",
    "The eight envelope-source tabs expose the two native envelopes, two real LFO envelopes and four LFO waveform views. ADSR fields follow the selected source; native envelope mode is disabled where that mode does not exist.",
    "The lower LFO editor independently selects LFO 1–4 and rebinds its real shape, rate, trigger, phase and fade controls. Source names and units remain native.",
    "Six primary macros occupy the measured top-right strip. Their assigned names remain live and their numeric values remain available through tooltip, typed entry and accessibility. Macros 7–8 and additional scene/ring controls remain available in the full editor, preserving the empty lower-right area of the reference.",
    "The eight effect cards select actual slots and rebind the algorithm menu and seven detail parameters. The selected-slot pictogram is an algorithm-family icon, not an asserted live transfer function or impulse response.",
    "Actual oscillator power/mute controls and catalog-backed wavetable previous/next/menu controls occupy the reference title rows. Sample/Granular algorithms or independent fine-pitch parameters are not fabricated.",
    "The output spectrum and channel meters use the independent real main-output tap. Inactive streams remain inactive. Filter curves are response previews of the actual filter/subtype and controls retain cutoff, resonance, keytracking and envelope amount semantics.",
    "Native scene/polyphony menus remain in the lower-left utility strip where the concept uses oscillator-family navigation. Full editor, preset, scene, skin and analyzer actions remain available through the native header and panel navigation."
  ]
}
